# PosterChanOS notification popups.
#
# WHY A DAEMON EXISTS AT ALL. The desktop calls Electron's Notification API for a DM, a mention or a
# call (desktop/main.js `pc:host:notify`, reached from app.js `osNotify`). On Linux that is libnotify
# talking to org.freedesktop.Notifications -- and PosterChanOS shipped neither the library nor a
# server, so `Notification.isSupported()` answered false, the bridge returned false, and every
# notification this desktop has ever raised was dropped in silence while Settings reported
# "granted". Measured on the running machine: `Unable to find libnotify; notifications disabled`.
#
# WHY NOT DRAW IT IN THE SHELL. PosterChan's own notification centre is a popup WINDOW, which is
# right for a list you open. A transient popup is the opposite case: it has to appear over whatever
# is on screen, including a fullscreen native application, and the shell surface is the TILED window
# underneath every one of those. mako is a layer-shell client, so the compositor stacks it above all
# of them -- the same reason the start menu had to stop being a div.
#
# This is not a second panel/dock/launcher/background: PosterChanUI still owns the taskbar, the
# desktop, the tray and the notification centre. mako draws nothing until something notifies.
#
# Portage owns this file; per-account overrides go in ~/.config/mako/config.
max-visible=4
sort=-time
layer=overlay
anchor=top-right
margin=12
padding=14
border-size=2
border-radius=10
width=380
height=180
default-timeout=8000
ignore-timeout=0
font=sans 11
# The compositor's own decoration colours, so a notification reads as part of this desktop.
background-color=#171222f2
text-color=#e9e4f5ff
border-color=#241438ff
progress-color=over #3a2260ff

[urgency=critical]
border-color=#c0392bff
default-timeout=0
